# serve.transcript -- the production tool's answers, pinned: one request a line, its answer the next.
#
# Kit_serve answers these today (ocaml/engine/kit/kit_serve.ml), and test_transcript.ml replays
# every one through `serve_line` (`eff serve`) and `mcp_line` (`eff mcp`), byte for byte. It is the
# net under the kit's move onto generated names (seat GEN, phase 1) and under the lowered
# transition of slice 1.7: an answer that moves fails the test at its line.
#
#   both> REQUEST   a command request: through serve_line, and through mcp_line as the tools/call
#                   of its op, whose text must be the same answer
#   serve> LINE     a line no tool call can carry, through serve_line only
#   mcp> MESSAGE    a JSON-RPC message, through mcp_line only
#   < ANSWER        the answer to the line above; "< (no reply)" for a message that gets none
#
# Never edit an answer by hand. A deliberate change of answer is one reviewed diff:
#   cd ocaml && E4_KIT_TRANSCRIPT_REWRITE=$PWD/engine/test/kit/serve.transcript \
#     opam exec --switch=effect4 -- dune test --force engine/test/kit

